course: dictionary
lesson: 15787
title: Unacceptable: not allowed, not good enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something must not happen. Unacceptable is one of them. It means not good enough or not allowed, so it cannot be accepted. «Running in the corridor is unacceptable» tells you the rule: stop running, because it is not allowed.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Hitting your friend is unacceptable. Teachers will always stop it.» The sentence tells you that hitting is wrong. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Hitting is not allowed» fits, so unacceptable means not allowed.
explain: The word is strong. Teachers, parents and leaders use it when they want to show that something is wrong and must change. «Totally unacceptable» and «completely unacceptable» make it even stronger. In maths or science, «an unacceptable error» is one that is too far off to use.
fact: Unacceptable means not good enough or not allowed, so it cannot be accepted.
fact: «Unacceptable behaviour» is behaviour that is wrong and must stop, like bullying or hitting.
fact: «Swearing at a teacher is unacceptable.» Here the rule is clear: it is not allowed.
fact: Leaders call things unacceptable to show strong disapproval.
fact: In maths and science, «an unacceptable answer» is one that is too far off to be useful.
exercise: «Bullying other children is unacceptable.» What does unacceptable mean here? | Fine, as long as nobody notices | *Not allowed, and must stop | Easy to do | Very funny
exercise: Jayden's answer is 500, but it should be 5. His teacher says it is an unacceptable error. What does she mean? | It is a kind mistake | It is correct but very long | It is a lucky guess | *It is too far off to be used
exercise: «Leaving litter in the park is unacceptable.» Find and copy one word that means not allowed. | *unacceptable | park | leaving | litter
test: «The referee said the foul was unacceptable.» What does the referee mean? | The foul was so quick nobody saw it | *The foul is not allowed | The foul gave the team a lucky start | The foul was a lovely goal
test: Why might a teacher say, «Unacceptable behaviour must stop»? | *Because the behaviour is wrong and not allowed | Because the behaviour is quiet | Because the behaviour has already finished | Because the behaviour is very popular
exam: Which sentence uses unacceptable correctly? | Drawing a picture is unacceptable. | Sharing your snack with a friend is unacceptable. | Reading a book quietly is unacceptable. | *Hitting a friend to get your own way is unacceptable.
